    "description": "``and`` is the logical operator of the same name. It returns ``true`` only when both operands are ``true``; otherwise, it returns ``false``. \n\nIt is a synonym for the symbolic operator ``&&``, though it has a different precedence level.\n\nThere is also a bitwise ``and`` operator: ``&``\n\n``and`` is a PHP keyword.",
